1
00:01:40,039 --> 00:01:40,840
Mala.

2
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:45,680
Mala.

3
00:01:52,720 --> 00:01:53,520
Mala.

4
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:00,960
Mala.

5
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:21,930
Bullying doesn't disappear as we grow up.

6
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:24,079
It just changes its form

7
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:25,650
and hides around us.

8
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:28,220
Many people don't really care

9
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:30,280
why bullying happens.

10
00:02:30,960 --> 00:02:33,640
They just tirelessly try to make those who expose the truth

11
00:02:33,640 --> 00:02:34,960
and reveal their pain

12
00:02:35,720 --> 00:02:36,400
shut up.

13
00:02:53,360 --> 00:02:54,490
What happened next?

14
00:02:55,440 --> 00:02:56,400
Where did he go?

15
00:02:58,680 --> 00:03:00,680
Time Travel Rule No. 3:

16
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:06,490
If two versions of yourself from different timelines meet,

17
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:08,850
it triggers the grandfather paradox.

18
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:12,560
The universe's timeline

19
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:13,840
will correct itself.

20
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:18,530
Mala, right before my eyes,

21
00:03:20,720 --> 00:03:21,920
disappeared.

22
00:03:26,640 --> 00:03:27,800
Am I the killer?

23
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:32,000
If I am the killer...

24
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:35,840
Then what about you?

25
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:37,560
I love my son.

26
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:39,840
And my son loves me too.

27
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:44,930
Don't think I'll forgive you just because you said this.

28
00:03:46,560 --> 00:03:49,000
I don't believe in any creepy nursery rhymes

29
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,560
or time travel.

30
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:54,530
You'd better tell me the truth.

31
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:58,960
What I said is the truth.

32
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:01,080
Admit it.

33
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:05,840
You don't want the truth at all.

34
00:04:06,440 --> 00:04:08,440
You just need an excuse

35
00:04:08,560 --> 00:04:10,480
to get rid of your guilt.

36
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:13,800
Actually, you know very well

37
00:04:14,360 --> 00:04:15,480
that for his death,

38
00:04:16,120 --> 00:04:17,240
you are also responsible.

39
00:04:17,240 --> 00:04:18,160
Shut up.

40
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:23,760
When he was alive,

41
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,240
you never really cared about him

42
00:04:26,440 --> 00:04:27,640
or understood him.

43
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,320
After he died,

44
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:31,720
you spent ten years seeking revenge.

45
00:04:32,080 --> 00:04:33,480
What's the point of that?

46
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:37,080
What's the point?

47
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:42,920
Fine.

48
00:04:43,560 --> 00:04:44,280
Fine.

49
00:04:44,720 --> 00:04:45,640
You're right.

50
00:04:47,159 --> 00:04:48,000
Then today,

51
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:50,170
let the two of us go together

52
00:04:51,760 --> 00:04:53,440
and apologize to Mala.

53
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:07,760
Life

54
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:11,000
is a game of Snake.

55
00:05:12,440 --> 00:05:13,800
If you don't eat others,

56
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:17,080
others will eat you.

57
00:05:18,280 --> 00:05:19,880
A killing blade never tires,

58
00:05:20,080 --> 00:05:21,080
but a human heart

59
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:21,960
will die,

60
00:05:22,560 --> 00:05:23,280
turn black,

61
00:05:23,760 --> 00:05:24,360
and rot.

62
00:05:25,160 --> 00:05:27,020
Every wrong has its perpetrator.

63
00:05:27,560 --> 00:05:28,880
A life for a life.

64
00:05:29,960 --> 00:05:31,960
There are 80,000 words in the world,

65
00:05:32,440 --> 00:05:34,370
but the word 'love' alone can kill.

66
00:05:35,880 --> 00:05:37,760
You stole my success,

67
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:38,800
my lover,

68
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:41,400
and my life. You can never repay me.

69
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:46,560
You look very tired.

70
00:05:49,240 --> 00:05:51,760
How on earth can I escape from here?

71
00:05:53,080 --> 00:05:53,880
Give up.

72
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:56,280
No one can escape this curse.

73
00:06:09,280 --> 00:06:10,800
Before turning into a dragon,

74
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:11,800
every little fish

75
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:14,320
will face the greatest malice and questioning.

76
00:06:14,320 --> 00:06:16,160
Why are you the one who leaped over the dragon gate?

77
00:06:16,160 --> 00:06:16,920
Why?

78
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:28,480
When I was a child,

79
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:31,450
I thought talent was the answer to this question.

80
00:06:31,880 --> 00:06:32,680
When I grew up,

81
00:06:32,880 --> 00:06:34,810
I thought hard work was the answer.

82
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:35,920
Later,

83
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:37,940
entering the adult world,

84
00:06:38,560 --> 00:06:40,290
I thought the answer was money,

85
00:06:40,320 --> 00:06:41,120
connections,

86
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:42,020
endurance,

87
00:06:42,200 --> 00:06:43,130
or taking risks.

88
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:46,330
But at this moment, I finally realize.

89
00:06:46,880 --> 00:06:48,480
A fish that has leaped over the dragon gate

90
00:06:48,480 --> 00:06:49,920
doesn't need an answer.

91
00:06:50,080 --> 00:06:52,200
He will also be worshipped by thousands.

92
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:53,440
Shining brightly.

93
00:06:53,960 --> 00:06:55,400
Only those who are alone,

94
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:57,080
losers with nothing,

95
00:06:57,360 --> 00:07:00,290
have had thousands of wrong answers in their hearts.

96
00:07:00,960 --> 00:07:02,090
But every one of them

97
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:04,130
deserves to be seen.

98
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:05,640
Unforgettable.

99
00:07:07,280 --> 00:07:09,210
Have you heard of the curse of time?

100
00:07:09,960 --> 00:07:10,960
An infinite loop,

101
00:07:11,480 --> 00:07:12,810
with nowhere to escape.

102
00:07:13,520 --> 00:07:14,120
Mala.

103
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:16,680
I also want to see what lies

104
00:07:17,040 --> 00:07:18,040
in the gap of time.

105
00:07:38,480 --> 00:07:39,880
Is this the afterlife?

106
00:07:41,040 --> 00:07:41,970
You're not dead.

107
00:07:59,880 --> 00:08:00,810
Long time no see.

108
00:08:02,840 --> 00:08:03,720
I didn't expect

109
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:07,250
my dad to cause you so much trouble.

110
00:08:11,040 --> 00:08:12,240
He made me realize

111
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:15,260
that not being good enough

112
00:08:15,320 --> 00:08:16,240
or bad enough,

113
00:08:17,360 --> 00:08:19,360
living in the middle is the hardest.

114
00:08:19,960 --> 00:08:20,960
I don't blame him.

115
00:08:23,200 --> 00:08:25,530
If I had bravely taken that step back then,

116
00:08:26,640 --> 00:08:28,640
admitted we were friends in public,

117
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:30,620
even if we got beaten up together,

118
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:33,799
the result might have been better than now.

119
00:08:36,720 --> 00:08:37,840
Later, I

120
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:42,659
immersed myself in chasing selfish dreams.

121
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:47,820
I thought I was absolutely right,

122
00:08:49,040 --> 00:08:51,370
thinking that after getting everything,

123
00:08:51,640 --> 00:08:54,040
I could come back and make it up to everyone.

124
00:08:55,760 --> 00:08:56,820
But in the process,

125
00:08:57,600 --> 00:08:59,330
I lost my most important friend

126
00:09:00,560 --> 00:09:01,690
and my closest love.

127
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:04,600
For fame, wealth,

128
00:09:05,080 --> 00:09:05,800
and desire,

129
00:09:07,160 --> 00:09:08,290
I let go of my dignity

130
00:09:09,560 --> 00:09:10,960
and abandoned my morals.

131
00:09:12,120 --> 00:09:13,000
Even friends

132
00:09:13,480 --> 00:09:14,280
and loved ones

133
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:16,130
could be discarded.

134
00:09:17,040 --> 00:09:19,170
Greedily taking from those around you

135
00:09:20,400 --> 00:09:21,640
will make you lose more,

136
00:09:21,640 --> 00:09:22,970
more important things.

137
00:09:25,320 --> 00:09:26,520
So God

138
00:09:27,800 --> 00:09:29,720
let me die on the eve of my success

139
00:09:33,760 --> 00:09:35,360
as a warning and protection.

140
00:09:42,280 --> 00:09:42,960
Mala.

141
00:09:48,760 --> 00:09:49,640
Thank you.

142
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:54,040
And,

143
00:09:57,320 --> 00:09:58,120
I'm sorry.

144
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:04,240
It's okay.

145
00:10:05,760 --> 00:10:07,220
I never blamed you anyway.

146
00:10:11,600 --> 00:10:13,330
It's just that where I'm going,

147
00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:17,300
there's no place for you anymore.

148
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:20,170
And your story isn't finished yet.

149
00:10:23,320 --> 00:10:24,120
Keep it up.

150
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:26,400
You're really talented.

151
00:10:28,120 --> 00:10:28,960
Keep going.

152
00:10:29,920 --> 00:10:31,050
I'll read your book.

153
00:10:33,600 --> 00:10:34,280
Zhiwei.

154
00:10:35,920 --> 00:10:37,440
I've made my choice.

155
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:40,560
Now it's your turn.

156
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:43,170
To stay in the dream,

157
00:10:44,320 --> 00:10:45,720
or to keep living.
